1). I kept the buggy read and reproduced the aliasing by storing all three tables in one contiguous blob in the C layout (`mixed@0, short@320, long@640`), so `mixed[8]` aliases `short[0]` and `short[8]` aliases `long[0]` exactly as in C.\n\nWorth flagging: this OOB row is **toolchain-dependent** in C — gcc `-O2/-O3` emits the order mixed/short/long, while gcc `-O0` and clang emit long/short/mixed. So no single stable C behavior exists for `sr_idx == 8`. I matched the optimized/Release layout; all **in-bounds** indices (0–7) are identical under every build. This is documented in the source.\n\n## Verification (differential, against the real C `.so`)\n| Test | Cases | Mismatches |\n|---|---|---|\n| Random fuzz (headers + bitstream + pos/limit) | 400,000 | **0** |\n| Exhaustive sweep of `hdr[1]`×`hdr[2]`×`hdr[3]` quadrant | 1,048,576 | **0** |\n| Edge cases (negative pos, `INT_MAX`/`INT_MIN` limits) × 6 C builds | 663,000 each | **0** |\n| `sfbtab` pointer offsets, all 9 `sr_idx` × 3 window modes | 27 | **0** |\n\nComparison was byte-level over the whole `L3_gr_info_t` array plus return value and mutated `bs` fields, with `sfbtab` compared by *content* and by *offset from table base* (addresses necessarily differ). Coverage confirmed all `sr_idx` 0–8, all block types 0–3, both mixed-block flags, and all three window tables. Also cross-checked against gcc `-O0/-O2/-O3` and clang `-O0/-O2` C builds — all agree.\n\n`cargo build --release` compiles clean with zero warnings, producing `translation/target/release/libtranslation.so`. `c_src/` is unmodified (original mtimes intact), and my scratch build directory was removed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_read_input_tokens":70110,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":433,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8130ce93-